{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ונגש", :translit "ve-nagash", :gloss "and he shall draw near"} {:he "ונגש הכהן", :translit "ve-nagash ha-kohen", :gloss "and the priest shall draw near"} {:he "ונגש חורש בקוצר", :translit "ve-nagash choresh ba-kotzer", :gloss "and the plowman shall draw near to the reaper"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ונגש" "ונגש הכהן" "ונגש חורש בקוצר"]}], :frame {:text "On Yom Kippur the high priest enters the Holy of Holies alone to pray for the year's success (Yoma 2a, 70b). Amos 9:13 depicts abundance with the image 'the plowman shall draw near to the reaper.' The midrashic method links rare word-occurrences across verses to draw structural analogies; here Moses' solitary ascent at Sinai is compared to the priest's solitary entry on Yom Kippur.", :sources ["Yoma 2a" "Yoma 70b" "Amos 9:13" "Exodus 24:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יגשו", :translit "yigshu", :gloss "they shall draw near"} {:he "והם לא יגשו", :translit "ve-hem lo yigshu", :gloss "but they shall not draw near"} {:he "אחד באחד יגשו", :translit "echad be-echad yigshu", :gloss "they shall draw near one by one"} {:he "משה מחיצה לעצמו", :translit "Moshe mechitzah le-atzmo", :gloss "Moses — a partition for himself"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["והם לא יגשו" "אחד באחד יגשו"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'Moses — a partition for himself' introduces a Tannaitic teaching that at Sinai Moses separated himself from Aaron, Aaron from the priests, and the priests from Israel, each at his own designated boundary (Rashi on Exodus 24:2 citing Mekhilta). The expression 'one by one' is read to mean that each person enters further in than his fellow, reflecting the graded levels of access established at Sinai.", :sources ["Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael" "Rashi on Exodus 24:2" "Exodus 24:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ונגש" "ונגש הכהן" "ונגש חורש בקוצר"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ונגש", :refs ["Exodu